Migrate algebra construction to the Rust side

Introduce an `algebra/` submodule on the Rust side that will eventually
host the per-statement morphism / structure construction currently
performed in eqlog.eql. The new pass is intended to assign one morphism
per statement (collapsing the per-branch-path fan-out the eqlog.eql
implementation produces today).

This branch starts with `algebra::signature`: dependent signatures over
types, predicates and functions, together with a pass that walks the
AST and builds a `Signature` from it. Not yet wired into the build.
